1
00:01:08,260 --> 00:01:12,723
Ma’am, prepare a treat,
remove the muzzle,

2
00:01:13,098 --> 00:01:15,726
and then give it to him.

3
00:01:22,566 --> 00:01:23,609
It’s alright.

4
00:01:30,449 --> 00:01:32,368
No! Get over here.

5
00:01:33,327 --> 00:01:34,462
Seung jae, stay there.

6
00:01:34,665 --> 00:01:36,566
Oh dear. The poor thing

7
00:01:36,590 --> 00:01:37,633
Stay still.

8
00:01:38,040 --> 00:01:40,021
What about the person who
gets bitten?

9
00:01:40,045 --> 00:01:41,046
What?

10
00:01:41,502 --> 00:01:43,587
Didn’t this hurt?

11
00:01:45,214 --> 00:01:47,383
Maybe just a little.

12
00:01:52,513 --> 00:01:54,223
Be strong.

13
00:01:55,975 --> 00:01:58,185
Think of all the effort
you’ve put into this.

14
00:02:03,899 --> 00:02:05,943
Shall we give it another try?

15
00:02:10,364 --> 00:02:11,471
- Good morning.
- Hello.

16
00:02:11,495 --> 00:02:12,830
You’re here early.

17
00:02:13,867 --> 00:02:15,516
Don’t forget we have training later.

18
00:02:15,540 --> 00:02:16,624
- Won’t you?!
- I won’t.

19
00:02:17,955 --> 00:02:19,665
- Good morning.
- Morning.

20
00:02:20,416 --> 00:02:23,294
Oh, Yukdeok!
That’s much better.

21
00:02:31,176 --> 00:02:32,594
They took them all already?

22
00:02:34,305 --> 00:02:35,996
Sure, they left this morning.

23
00:02:36,020 --> 00:02:38,022
Didn’t even have a chance
to say goodbye.

24
00:02:39,643 --> 00:02:45,190
You know, I love this tranquility
we get once in a while.

25
00:02:46,025 --> 00:02:48,841
All these dogs with broken hearts here.

26
00:02:48,865 --> 00:02:50,992
Abused and abandoned.

27
00:02:51,989 --> 00:02:55,075
Now they’ve found good homes.
Isn’t that great?

28
00:02:56,535 --> 00:02:58,287
Depends on the person.

29
00:02:58,829 --> 00:03:00,640
<i>Tout va bien.</i>

30
00:03:00,664 --> 00:03:04,209
Just leave it to me.
I run a tight ship here.

31
00:03:32,905 --> 00:03:37,326
<i>From Lee Sora</i>
<i>Cheongsan Women’s Correctional Facility</i>

32
00:03:54,593 --> 00:03:57,864
<i>The era of 10 million pets.</i>
<i>Lee Hayoung joins us…</i>

33
00:03:57,888 --> 00:03:58,948
It’s starting.

34
00:03:58,972 --> 00:04:03,936
<i>…to talk us through how we can share a life</i>
<i>with our canine friends.</i>

35
00:04:04,003 --> 00:04:05,004
<i>Welcome.</i>

36
00:04:05,204 --> 00:04:05,933
<i>Hello.</i>

37
00:04:05,957 --> 00:04:07,142
<i>Nice to meet you.</i>

38
00:04:07,439 --> 00:04:10,524
<i>Is there a way to prevent</i>
<i>dog bite incidents?</i>

39
00:04:10,901 --> 00:04:12,444
<i>Yes.</i>

40
00:04:13,112 --> 00:04:14,798
Why? You look great.

41
00:04:14,822 --> 00:04:16,990
Hey, stop watching it.

42
00:04:17,491 --> 00:04:19,493
You were born to be on TV.

43
00:04:20,327 --> 00:04:22,204
You get used to it.

44
00:04:24,373 --> 00:04:25,707
How about a foot massage?

45
00:04:26,333 --> 00:04:29,169
No, not my foot…

46
00:04:43,559 --> 00:04:44,643
Hayoung.

47
00:04:44,810 --> 00:04:45,869
Hmm?

48
00:04:46,186 --> 00:04:48,730
I was thinking about the room
on the second floor.

49
00:04:50,399 --> 00:04:53,444
You said you were going to use it
as your study.

50
00:04:57,948 --> 00:05:01,118
A room for a baby.
Should we try for it?

51
00:05:03,996 --> 00:05:05,056
A baby?

52
00:05:05,080 --> 00:05:06,165
Yeah.

53
00:05:12,129 --> 00:05:14,023
- Wait.
- Why?

54
00:05:14,047 --> 00:05:16,091
Wait. Wait.

55
00:05:16,800 --> 00:05:17,968
Oh…

56
00:05:32,357 --> 00:05:39,448
<i>Dog Owners Require Training</i>

57
00:06:08,018 --> 00:06:14,441
<i>Cheongsan Women’s Correctional Facility</i>

58
00:07:01,572 --> 00:07:05,325
- <i>Dogs are mirrors of their owners</i>
<i>- Dog Behaviorist Lee Hayoung</i>

59
00:07:07,286 --> 00:07:09,806
Excuse me… Can I help you?

60
00:07:09,830 --> 00:07:10,831
Huh?

61
00:07:17,462 --> 00:07:18,839
Where is she?

62
00:07:24,261 --> 00:07:25,262
Hey!

63
00:07:26,805 --> 00:07:28,432
She’s not answering.

64
00:07:29,099 --> 00:07:31,435
She should be back soon.
Will you wait for her?

65
00:07:32,269 --> 00:07:34,563
Sure. I’m in no rush.

66
00:07:35,314 --> 00:07:36,815
Want something to drink?

67
00:07:54,666 --> 00:07:56,126
Freedom!

68
00:08:01,173 --> 00:08:02,446
Do you have a dog?

69
00:08:02,470 --> 00:08:05,056
As if! You can’t have dogs there.

70
00:08:06,261 --> 00:08:09,056
Oh, I guess that’s not
allowed at your place.

71
00:08:09,473 --> 00:08:12,976
Then did you raise a dog before?

72
00:08:13,644 --> 00:08:15,103
Before?

73
00:08:16,355 --> 00:08:18,565
You could say that.

74
00:08:19,441 --> 00:08:21,735
Did I raise it…?
Yeah, I guess.

75
00:08:22,653 --> 00:08:24,363
But it died.

76
00:08:30,077 --> 00:08:31,578
What’s that thing?

77
00:08:32,037 --> 00:08:33,514
This?

78
00:08:33,538 --> 00:08:38,418
It’s a pet microchip.
It’s like a Social Security number.

79
00:08:39,961 --> 00:08:41,505
So harsh…

80
00:08:42,297 --> 00:08:43,507
Sorry?

81
00:08:44,591 --> 00:08:46,093
You heard me.

82
00:08:46,426 --> 00:08:48,053
It’s not a bad thing.

83
00:08:48,679 --> 00:08:51,536
It helps you find your dog
if it goes missing.

84
00:08:51,560 --> 00:08:52,895
Uh-huh.

85
00:09:07,322 --> 00:09:11,284
By the way,
how do you know Hayoung?

86
00:09:14,371 --> 00:09:16,039
Look at my face.

87
00:09:20,544 --> 00:09:22,337
Don’t I remind you of anyone?

88
00:09:50,866 --> 00:09:55,704
You refused all my visits.
Why the sudden change of heart?

89
00:09:57,414 --> 00:10:02,210
Sudden?
I sent you tons of letters.

90
00:10:24,733 --> 00:10:27,360
You call an empty envelope a letter?

91
00:10:36,870 --> 00:10:40,290
Sis, how about a job?

92
00:10:56,097 --> 00:10:58,809
7 years and that’s the first thing
you’ve gotta say?

93
00:10:59,476 --> 00:11:03,688
Sure, it’s your company.
Just hire me.

94
00:11:04,731 --> 00:11:06,630
Do you know what we do here?

95
00:11:06,654 --> 00:11:08,447
Yeah, you train dogs.

96
00:11:09,736 --> 00:11:13,573
But damn, you’re so famous now!

97
00:11:13,865 --> 00:11:15,867
I was floored.

98
00:11:22,499 --> 00:11:24,376
You’re scared of dogs.

99
00:11:25,585 --> 00:11:28,981
That was before.
I freaking love dogs.

100
00:11:29,005 --> 00:11:32,384
Loving them isn’t enough.
This is real work.

101
00:11:37,138 --> 00:11:38,265
So is that a yes?

102
00:11:38,598 --> 00:11:40,684
It’s a job, not a joke.

103
00:11:44,020 --> 00:11:45,564
I’m serious.

104
00:11:52,279 --> 00:11:53,363
Why?

105
00:11:55,198 --> 00:11:56,449
You need new clothes.

106
00:12:01,371 --> 00:12:02,622
Come on.

107
00:12:16,052 --> 00:12:17,345
What are you doing?

108
00:12:19,180 --> 00:12:20,807
- Woo hoo!
- Hey!

109
00:12:58,595 --> 00:13:00,513
- This is it.
- Sick!

110
00:13:01,681 --> 00:13:03,284
This place is wild.

111
00:13:03,308 --> 00:13:04,559
What?

112
00:13:18,490 --> 00:13:19,866
It’s all new.

113
00:13:20,241 --> 00:13:23,763
We turned it into my husband’s study
but he never uses it.

114
00:13:23,787 --> 00:13:25,205
What does he do?

115
00:13:29,960 --> 00:13:33,630
His book.
Read it if you want.

116
00:13:42,806 --> 00:13:44,891
It’s late. Get some rest.

117
00:13:45,725 --> 00:13:46,977
Yes, ma’am.

118
00:13:51,940 --> 00:13:53,316
Don’t close it.

119
00:13:53,817 --> 00:13:55,610
I don’t wanna feel locked in.

120
00:13:57,153 --> 00:13:59,739
You make it sound like
I kidnapped you.

121
00:14:16,881 --> 00:14:19,300
How could you do this
without running it by me?

122
00:14:20,093 --> 00:14:22,804
You expect me to leave my sister
out on the street?

123
00:14:27,267 --> 00:14:30,705
We’re partners.
You should’ve told me.

124
00:14:30,729 --> 00:14:33,648
Tell you what?
That she was in jail?

125
00:14:34,607 --> 00:14:36,526
J… jail?

126
00:14:50,623 --> 00:14:52,208
Murder.

127
00:14:53,376 --> 00:14:54,603
Huh?

128
00:14:54,627 --> 00:14:56,046
She killed someone.

129
00:14:56,713 --> 00:14:57,881
- What?
- Quiet!

130
00:14:58,965 --> 00:15:00,925
I left the door open.

131
00:15:03,678 --> 00:15:06,890
Well then help me to understand!

132
00:15:08,892 --> 00:15:11,644
She stabbed some guy
who tried to rape her.

133
00:15:17,609 --> 00:15:18,777
Wait.

134
00:15:20,195 --> 00:15:22,363
Isn’t that self-defense?

135
00:15:24,991 --> 00:15:29,245
They didn’t see it that way.
Too many stab wounds.

136
00:16:00,401 --> 00:16:02,403
Fuck! You scared me.

137
00:16:05,698 --> 00:16:07,784
What are you doing here?

138
00:16:09,244 --> 00:16:11,412
Wanted to check in on you.

139
00:16:12,038 --> 00:16:13,390
Have a nightmare?

140
00:16:13,414 --> 00:16:14,582
Yeah!

141
00:16:21,047 --> 00:16:24,092
Here? No way.

142
00:16:31,474 --> 00:16:33,101
It wasn’t my fault.

143
00:16:35,770 --> 00:16:38,731
I could’ve died
if I hadn’t done anything.

144
00:16:48,074 --> 00:16:51,119
I know, how mistreated you feel.

145
00:16:53,997 --> 00:16:55,165
Do you?

146
00:16:57,709 --> 00:16:59,961
Forget those bad memories.

147
00:17:00,211 --> 00:17:01,921
Put the past behind you.

148
00:17:05,717 --> 00:17:07,218
Forget…

149
00:17:16,936 --> 00:17:18,021
Sis.

150
00:17:19,772 --> 00:17:26,571
If our house hadn’t burned down,
would we have stayed together?

151
00:17:31,034 --> 00:17:33,953
Maybe we wouldn’t be living
so far apart.

152
00:17:39,125 --> 00:17:41,252
I don’t remember the accident.

153
00:17:41,628 --> 00:17:43,171
And I don’t want to.

154
00:17:46,883 --> 00:17:48,134
Of course.

155
00:17:50,220 --> 00:17:53,014
So you’re saying you don’t remember
what happened?

156
00:18:08,029 --> 00:18:12,492
I want to be human,
just like you.

157
00:18:15,870 --> 00:18:17,580
How do you do it?

158
00:19:06,754 --> 00:19:09,132
Do I really have to run
every morning?

159
00:19:09,590 --> 00:19:11,860
You said you wanna live like
a human being.

160
00:19:11,884 --> 00:19:13,720
You can start by being healthy.

161
00:19:13,886 --> 00:19:15,221
I am healthy.

162
00:19:16,306 --> 00:19:18,516
No you’re not.
Hurry up.

163
00:19:31,779 --> 00:19:34,949
Do I seriously have to clean up shit
every morning?

164
00:19:37,618 --> 00:19:39,954
That’s a trainer’s basic duty.

165
00:19:40,455 --> 00:19:43,183
And you have to
keep an eye on it too.

166
00:19:43,207 --> 00:19:46,294
If it looks or smells strange,
be sure to let me know.

167
00:19:47,378 --> 00:19:49,481
So when the hell do I get to train?

168
00:19:49,505 --> 00:19:51,066
You’re an apprentice.

169
00:19:51,090 --> 00:19:54,361
You’ll be doing cleaning and odd jobs
for at least 3 months.

170
00:19:54,385 --> 00:19:55,445
Seriously?

171
00:20:01,267 --> 00:20:02,643
By the way…

172
00:20:04,145 --> 00:20:05,480
what’s with the attitude?

173
00:20:09,442 --> 00:20:12,320
Chill out, dude.
We’re the same age.

174
00:20:16,699 --> 00:20:17,801
Is it true?

175
00:20:17,825 --> 00:20:18,951
What?

176
00:20:20,036 --> 00:20:23,915
That you’re Hayoung’s sister.
You’re so different.

177
00:20:24,499 --> 00:20:26,834
We’re like basically the same.

178
00:20:32,131 --> 00:20:33,633
I don’t see it.

179
00:20:36,969 --> 00:20:39,305
Guess you only see
what you wanna see.

180
00:20:47,146 --> 00:20:49,065
I’ll be back in an hour.

181
00:21:09,127 --> 00:21:11,730
Good girl. There there.

182
00:21:11,754 --> 00:21:13,506
It’s okay.

183
00:21:17,009 --> 00:21:18,009
Let me see.

184
00:21:23,891 --> 00:21:26,286
How could you let this happen?

185
00:21:26,310 --> 00:21:29,623
Chocolate is poisonous for dogs.
You should know that.

186
00:21:29,647 --> 00:21:30,647
I’m sorry.

187
00:21:31,023 --> 00:21:32,775
I need to be able to trust you.

188
00:21:38,990 --> 00:21:42,368
What are you waiting for?
Get back to work.

189
00:21:45,746 --> 00:21:47,081
Yes, ma’am.

190
00:21:54,046 --> 00:21:55,798
What about Sora?

191
00:22:49,852 --> 00:22:51,103
What?

192
00:22:52,313 --> 00:22:53,898
What do you mean?

193
00:22:54,440 --> 00:22:56,234
Why are you looking at me?

194
00:22:57,818 --> 00:23:00,821
Umm… you’re looking at me too.

195
00:23:10,831 --> 00:23:13,960
Why is my door closed?
I left it open.

196
00:23:14,544 --> 00:23:19,632
Uh… Could’ve been the wind, I guess?

197
00:23:27,390 --> 00:23:31,644
Hey honey. What?

198
00:23:35,064 --> 00:23:39,860
He… hello?
No, it’s just me here.

199
00:23:43,698 --> 00:23:45,032
Bye.

200
00:23:49,412 --> 00:23:50,931
You’re a good liar.

201
00:23:50,955 --> 00:23:52,415
Is something going on?

202
00:23:53,541 --> 00:23:56,085
Feels like
I’m caught in the middle.

203
00:23:56,294 --> 00:23:58,689
Help me out
from time to time, okay?

204
00:23:58,713 --> 00:23:59,797
What?

205
00:24:02,592 --> 00:24:04,552
But I’m not a liar.

206
00:24:06,804 --> 00:24:09,932
Good practice for a writer though,
isn’t it?

207
00:24:10,474 --> 00:24:11,767
I liked your book.

208
00:24:13,227 --> 00:24:14,270
You read it?

209
00:24:15,980 --> 00:24:17,732
You really read my book?

210
00:25:29,929 --> 00:25:34,159
<i>CCTV & Hidden Camera Installation</i>

211
00:25:34,183 --> 00:25:39,188
<i>Suspect Lee arrested in brutal stabbing</i>
<i>of rapist for excessive self-defense</i>

212
00:26:04,672 --> 00:26:06,674
<i>Fucking piece of shit!</i>

213
00:26:18,644 --> 00:26:20,288
Guess I had to press it harder.

214
00:26:20,312 --> 00:26:22,940
No, longer. About 5 seconds.

215
00:26:38,205 --> 00:26:39,623
Hey.

216
00:26:41,208 --> 00:26:43,919
Your novel.
It’s all made up, right?

217
00:26:47,673 --> 00:26:50,176
Sure. It’s a novel.

218
00:26:50,801 --> 00:26:52,094
Whatever.

219
00:26:52,386 --> 00:26:57,308
Still, there’s research and interviews. A
lot of work goes into making it realistic.

220
00:26:58,017 --> 00:27:01,228
Why not write a real story
instead of a realistic one?

221
00:27:04,023 --> 00:27:05,858
You can get sued for that.

222
00:27:07,860 --> 00:27:10,154
Someone should totally write my story.

223
00:27:12,948 --> 00:27:14,178
You were tempted, right?

224
00:27:14,202 --> 00:27:14,827
Huh?

225
00:27:15,075 --> 00:27:19,163
Come on, interview me.
You’re curious about me.

226
00:27:22,124 --> 00:27:25,044
How can you be so sure?

227
00:27:26,962 --> 00:27:31,050
I feel the same.
I’m curious about you.

228
00:27:40,142 --> 00:27:41,286
Hey, Hayoung.

229
00:27:41,310 --> 00:27:43,103
- Could you…
- I got it.

230
00:27:43,521 --> 00:27:46,774
You look exhausted.
What’s that on your jacket?

231
00:27:48,067 --> 00:27:49,276
Have you eaten?

232
00:28:00,246 --> 00:28:01,956
Seriously? On your first day?

233
00:28:02,456 --> 00:28:03,541
What?

234
00:28:06,544 --> 00:28:09,463
A puppy nearly died thanks to
the chocolate you gave him.

235
00:28:10,923 --> 00:28:12,550
It wasn’t me.

236
00:28:13,259 --> 00:28:14,593
It wasn’t?

237
00:28:17,137 --> 00:28:20,641
Shit, did I drop some?

238
00:28:24,019 --> 00:28:26,272
This stuff can seriously kill dogs?

239
00:28:27,106 --> 00:28:28,816
In some cases, yes.

240
00:28:35,239 --> 00:28:36,448
So?

241
00:28:37,658 --> 00:28:39,618
You think I did it on purpose?

242
00:28:46,625 --> 00:28:47,625
No.

243
00:28:49,211 --> 00:28:52,131
You didn’t know
what would happen. Right?

244
00:28:52,798 --> 00:28:57,261
Of course! I love my chocolate.
Why would I give it to some dog?

245
00:29:00,222 --> 00:29:04,268
Sora, I trust you.

246
00:29:05,895 --> 00:29:07,855
But other people don’t know you.

247
00:29:09,815 --> 00:29:12,484
I’ll let it pass this time,
since it was a mistake.

248
00:29:26,749 --> 00:29:27,749
What’s that?

249
00:29:29,752 --> 00:29:33,923
Oh, the wall felt a bit empty.

250
00:29:34,715 --> 00:29:36,383
What do you think?

251
00:29:37,801 --> 00:29:39,553
Whatever. Up to you.

252
00:29:41,639 --> 00:29:44,642
This is your room now.
You get to decide.

253
00:29:48,938 --> 00:29:50,731
Straighten it up…

254
00:29:53,859 --> 00:29:54,985
Sis.

255
00:29:55,277 --> 00:29:56,320
Hmm?

256
00:29:58,489 --> 00:30:00,240
Do you really trust me?

257
00:30:07,790 --> 00:30:08,874
Yeah.

258
00:30:16,548 --> 00:30:17,967
Get some sleep.

259
00:30:23,055 --> 00:30:24,682
Your sister.

260
00:30:26,517 --> 00:30:29,019
She’s not as scary as I thought.

261
00:30:30,312 --> 00:30:31,689
You were scared?

262
00:30:32,856 --> 00:30:38,362
Frankly I wondered what you were thinking
bringing her home. I was angry.

263
00:30:40,030 --> 00:30:46,578
But then I realized
she’s the only family you have.

264
00:30:55,587 --> 00:30:58,590
I think you give her
what I’m not able to.

265
00:31:00,217 --> 00:31:01,468
Me?

266
00:31:03,971 --> 00:31:05,973
Lend her your ear, okay?

267
00:31:12,229 --> 00:31:14,648
But don’t believe everything she says.

268
00:32:03,363 --> 00:32:05,175
Want a refill?

269
00:32:05,199 --> 00:32:06,492
Nope.

270
00:32:25,260 --> 00:32:26,595
Mr. Writer.

271
00:32:35,020 --> 00:32:36,188
Yes?

272
00:32:38,148 --> 00:32:41,527
So how ’bout it?
My story as a novel.

273
00:32:45,322 --> 00:32:50,077
A woman in her 20s
stabbing her rapist to death…

274
00:32:51,161 --> 00:32:53,247
Can’t say I’m too interested.

275
00:32:55,582 --> 00:32:56,834
How come?

276
00:32:59,503 --> 00:33:01,505
Because he has to die.

277
00:33:03,340 --> 00:33:05,843
There’s no mystery.
No secrets.

278
00:33:07,594 --> 00:33:09,263
Ah…

279
00:33:11,265 --> 00:33:14,601
You need a story with a secret.

280
00:33:21,483 --> 00:33:22,501
Why?

281
00:33:23,485 --> 00:33:26,071
Funny story popped up in my mind.

282
00:33:27,573 --> 00:33:28,648
A real one.

283
00:33:29,825 --> 00:33:31,076
Tell me.

284
00:33:32,953 --> 00:33:34,788
My sister and I.

285
00:33:36,832 --> 00:33:38,750
So, what is it?

286
00:33:41,128 --> 00:33:43,213
Nah, what’s there to talk about.

287
00:33:43,589 --> 00:33:45,382
Forget I said anything.

288
00:33:46,175 --> 00:33:48,570
Don’t leave me hanging like that.

289
00:33:48,594 --> 00:33:52,848
If you’re curious, just ask her
about what happened to us.

290
00:33:57,436 --> 00:33:59,980
She doesn’t like to talk about
private things.

291
00:34:01,023 --> 00:34:03,358
Why would you marry
someone like that?

292
00:34:12,659 --> 00:34:16,955
Like it? You like it?
Want some more?

293
00:34:17,748 --> 00:34:19,082
Want more?

294
00:34:19,875 --> 00:34:23,879
Good boy.

295
00:34:26,590 --> 00:34:27,841
Hold on.

296
00:34:41,688 --> 00:34:43,440
Hey! Jelly!

297
00:34:44,066 --> 00:34:51,314
<i>The owner suffered a leg injury and his</i>
<i>8-month-old Maltese sadly died on the spot.</i>

298
00:34:51,823 --> 00:34:56,328
<i>When the owner came to his senses,</i>
<i>the dog who attacked him had disappeared.</i>

299
00:34:56,703 --> 00:35:02,042
<i>The victim’s family filed a police report,</i>
<i>but the dog is believed to be a stray.</i>

300
00:35:02,876 --> 00:35:07,130
<i>Police said they will set up a special team</i>
<i>to capture the dangerous animal.</i>

301
00:35:11,385 --> 00:35:13,905
You’re saying it’s Tofu?

302
00:35:13,929 --> 00:35:15,615
Why are you only saying this now?

303
00:35:15,639 --> 00:35:20,978
You were busy with your TV shows
and we were busy at the center.

304
00:35:21,436 --> 00:35:25,208
I tried looking for her for months,
but I couldn’t find her.

305
00:35:25,232 --> 00:35:29,528
But… that was like… 3 years ago.
Wasn’t it, Hayoung?

306
00:35:32,447 --> 00:35:36,326
A dog trained by a trainer
killed someone? If that got out…

307
00:35:36,994 --> 00:35:38,304
what do you think would happen?

308
00:35:38,328 --> 00:35:40,163
No one died!

309
00:35:40,872 --> 00:35:42,541
But someone could have.

310
00:35:42,749 --> 00:35:44,852
If Tofu keeps doing this and
gets caught,

311
00:35:44,876 --> 00:35:46,378
everyone will know.

312
00:35:47,546 --> 00:35:51,008
Her microchip.
It’s registered to our center.

313
00:35:52,801 --> 00:35:54,177
Right…

314
00:35:55,053 --> 00:35:59,158
You also reported her as adopted
even though she escaped.

315
00:35:59,182 --> 00:36:01,953
I couldn’t say we’d lost
another stray dog.

316
00:36:01,977 --> 00:36:04,646
Hayoung, I had to do that!

317
00:36:06,898 --> 00:36:09,359
Stop clicking that, would you?

318
00:36:16,533 --> 00:36:18,243
I’m not blaming you.

319
00:36:18,785 --> 00:36:19,953
Relax.

320
00:36:21,997 --> 00:36:28,754
Hayoung,
I never meant to deceive you. I…

321
00:36:29,838 --> 00:36:37,554
I did it for the center.
I just wanted to help you somehow, but…

322
00:36:39,598 --> 00:36:41,558
What should we do?

323
00:36:45,979 --> 00:36:47,814
What choice do we have?

324
00:36:48,690 --> 00:36:51,234
We have to catch her,
before anyone else.

325
00:36:52,652 --> 00:36:54,196
Catch her?

326
00:36:54,696 --> 00:36:55,989
Us?

327
00:36:56,948 --> 00:36:58,450
Who else?

328
00:36:59,868 --> 00:37:01,536
I trained her after all.

329
00:37:18,512 --> 00:37:21,390
Mingyeong, have you been drinking?

330
00:37:21,890 --> 00:37:23,183
No!

331
00:37:28,438 --> 00:37:30,232
Well, just one glass.

332
00:37:31,441 --> 00:37:35,320
This is our workplace.
You promised to quit.

333
00:37:36,238 --> 00:37:37,489
I’m sorry.

334
00:37:43,954 --> 00:37:45,473
Why are you here?

335
00:37:45,497 --> 00:37:48,750
You asked me to bring this.

336
00:37:52,337 --> 00:37:53,338
Put it there.

337
00:38:02,973 --> 00:38:04,617
Heading out for a rescue?

338
00:38:04,641 --> 00:38:05,851
Yes.

339
00:38:09,396 --> 00:38:10,689
Seungjae.

340
00:38:12,065 --> 00:38:14,067
You have a dart gun, right?

341
00:38:15,986 --> 00:38:16,987
Yes.

342
00:38:17,988 --> 00:38:19,406
Why?

343
00:38:26,371 --> 00:38:27,956
When I was young,

344
00:38:29,583 --> 00:38:32,878
me and my pals tried to
rob a store.

345
00:38:34,171 --> 00:38:36,548
But there was a dog there.

346
00:38:38,633 --> 00:38:42,846
It was really protective of its owner
and wouldn’t stop barking at us.

347
00:38:44,681 --> 00:38:46,892
But it looked so cool.

348
00:38:49,644 --> 00:38:52,898
That’s when I realized how cool it was
to protect something.

349
00:38:54,107 --> 00:38:57,402
I wanted to be like that dog.

350
00:38:58,403 --> 00:39:02,741
I wanted to have something
to protect like that.

351
00:39:09,790 --> 00:39:12,876
Oh, how did Tofu end up
in our center?

352
00:39:14,377 --> 00:39:16,838
She was rescued from a dog farm.

353
00:39:19,132 --> 00:39:20,675
It was horrible.

354
00:39:25,597 --> 00:39:26,640
I see.

355
00:39:41,696 --> 00:39:44,699
What about you?
Why do you do this?

356
00:39:47,494 --> 00:39:48,745
Me?

357
00:40:02,384 --> 00:40:04,010
I’m pretty good.

358
00:40:12,310 --> 00:40:14,288
I’m a fast learner, right?

359
00:40:14,312 --> 00:40:16,189
Most people get there in a year.

360
00:40:49,014 --> 00:40:50,807
Seungjae, you drive.

361
00:40:58,648 --> 00:41:00,334
What the…

362
00:41:00,358 --> 00:41:01,943
What’s wrong with her?

363
00:41:04,446 --> 00:41:06,072
She’s coming with us?

364
00:41:10,619 --> 00:41:13,496
Seungjae, go that way.
Mingyeong, follow me.

365
00:41:30,347 --> 00:41:32,015
What’s with her?

366
00:41:33,433 --> 00:41:35,977
Hayoung, look, footprints.

367
00:41:36,102 --> 00:41:37,330
Where?

368
00:41:37,354 --> 00:41:38,563
Here.

369
00:42:21,564 --> 00:42:22,941
Run!

370
00:42:31,991 --> 00:42:33,326
Tofu!

371
00:42:33,785 --> 00:42:35,078
Catch her!

372
00:43:02,689 --> 00:43:03,874
Should we get going?

373
00:43:03,898 --> 00:43:05,459
Your sister…

374
00:43:05,483 --> 00:43:08,278
doesn’t know about Tofu, right?

375
00:43:09,195 --> 00:43:10,864
What do you mean?

376
00:43:11,239 --> 00:43:13,658
It just felt like
she did it on purpose.

377
00:43:15,410 --> 00:43:20,498
There was the chocolate thing.
And she messed things up today too.

378
00:43:24,210 --> 00:43:25,920
It’s not like that.

379
00:43:26,421 --> 00:43:27,922
It was a mistake.

380
00:43:30,425 --> 00:43:33,553
You said you guys had a rough split
back in the day.

381
00:43:34,637 --> 00:43:36,240
Can we…

382
00:43:36,264 --> 00:43:38,099
really trust her?

383
00:43:39,768 --> 00:43:41,144
Yes.

384
00:43:44,481 --> 00:43:45,690
Are you mad?

385
00:43:48,860 --> 00:43:51,738
Good work today.
See you tomorrow.

386
00:44:24,354 --> 00:44:25,355
Did you catch her?

387
00:44:26,439 --> 00:44:27,607
No.

388
00:44:29,192 --> 00:44:30,860
Too bad.

389
00:44:32,862 --> 00:44:35,740
Mingyeong thinks
you did it on purpose.

390
00:44:36,783 --> 00:44:38,451
She hates my guts.

391
00:44:41,204 --> 00:44:42,389
Is it true?

392
00:44:42,413 --> 00:44:43,808
Yeah.

393
00:44:43,832 --> 00:44:45,726
I hate her too.
She’s gross.

394
00:44:45,750 --> 00:44:47,085
No.

395
00:44:49,921 --> 00:44:52,423
Did you do it on purpose?

396
00:44:53,216 --> 00:44:55,468
I don’t remember.
I panicked.

397
00:44:57,929 --> 00:45:00,265
But you get it, right?

398
00:45:01,724 --> 00:45:03,893
You panicked too.

399
00:45:04,811 --> 00:45:06,646
So you don’t remember.

400
00:45:11,150 --> 00:45:12,986
Just like last time, right?

401
00:46:28,269 --> 00:46:30,956
<i>Following the recent dog bite incident,</i>

402
00:46:30,980 --> 00:46:36,128
<i>reports of a stray dog roaming</i>
<i>the mountains of Myogyeong district</i>

403
00:46:36,152 --> 00:46:38,589
<i>have been making residents anxious.</i>

404
00:46:38,613 --> 00:46:41,592
<i>The city council has pledged to</i>
<i>send firefighters and</i>

405
00:46:41,616 --> 00:46:44,869
<i>a wildlife rescue team</i>
<i>to capture the animal.</i>

406
00:47:10,979 --> 00:47:12,105
Shall we?

407
00:47:12,772 --> 00:47:14,190
Where’s Mingyeong?

408
00:47:16,150 --> 00:47:17,527
Just us today.

409
00:47:20,947 --> 00:47:22,198
Sit shotgun.

410
00:48:17,503 --> 00:48:20,923
Oh, those… Can I explain?

411
00:48:22,550 --> 00:48:24,635
Sure, I’m all ears.

412
00:48:26,012 --> 00:48:31,184
I need to describe things when I write.
What they are, how they look.

413
00:48:31,350 --> 00:48:36,230
I can’t just imagine it all by myself,
so I need a model.

414
00:48:36,689 --> 00:48:38,691
You need ingredients
to make something.

415
00:48:40,068 --> 00:48:41,861
So what d’you make?

416
00:48:43,821 --> 00:48:45,615
Nothing just yet.

417
00:48:51,162 --> 00:48:52,789
I’ll delete them all.

418
00:48:55,166 --> 00:48:57,418
Could you keep it a secret
from Hayoung?

419
00:48:58,878 --> 00:49:00,338
What’s in it for me?

420
00:49:23,569 --> 00:49:26,572
I’m gonna take a look around.
Stay here.

421
00:49:27,865 --> 00:49:29,951
Don’t go too far.
It’s dangerous.

422
00:49:32,120 --> 00:49:33,913
For me, or you?

423
00:49:37,500 --> 00:49:38,793
I’ll be back.

424
00:50:44,692 --> 00:50:45,902
Sis.

425
00:50:51,449 --> 00:50:54,493
I wish I was stronger.

426
00:51:07,590 --> 00:51:13,471
You know, it’s my first time
drinking here since we moved in.

427
00:51:13,721 --> 00:51:14,889
Huh?

428
00:51:16,891 --> 00:51:18,476
Are you for real?

429
00:51:19,644 --> 00:51:22,980
No f-ing way I could hold back.

430
00:51:24,315 --> 00:51:25,399
Cheers.

431
00:51:26,108 --> 00:51:27,151
Cheers.

432
00:51:54,845 --> 00:51:56,264
Thank you.

433
00:52:49,400 --> 00:52:51,819
Hayoung and I used to do this
all the time.

434
00:53:47,541 --> 00:53:50,211
I think she knows.
She’s not taking the bait.

435
00:53:53,589 --> 00:53:55,383
Let’s give it a minute.

436
00:54:46,851 --> 00:54:48,436
I knew you’d come.

437
00:54:57,778 --> 00:54:59,280
Don’t close it.

438
00:54:59,572 --> 00:55:01,699
Hayoung’s not coming home today.

439
00:55:07,705 --> 00:55:09,039
Wide open!

440
00:57:28,596 --> 00:57:30,598
Why didn’t you wake me?

441
00:57:31,890 --> 00:57:35,603
Hang on, I’ll do it.

442
00:57:36,312 --> 00:57:38,856
It’s almost done.
Sleep well?

443
00:57:39,982 --> 00:57:40,983
Yeah.

444
00:57:41,442 --> 00:57:42,985
You were snoring.

445
00:57:43,277 --> 00:57:48,616
Really? I’m sorry.
Guess you couldn’t sleep.

446
00:57:49,700 --> 00:57:53,871
Just kidding.
How about a date tonight?

447
00:57:54,496 --> 00:57:58,042
A date, tonight? Us?

448
00:57:59,043 --> 00:58:01,295
Sure, why?
Don’t want to?

449
00:58:03,005 --> 00:58:04,381
I do,

450
00:58:05,049 --> 00:58:07,569
but I came up with a good idea
for my book.

451
00:58:07,593 --> 00:58:12,681
Want to submit by the end of month,
so my mind’s in a state.

452
00:58:14,975 --> 00:58:20,272
Good for you.
Sudden flash of inspiration?

453
00:58:21,398 --> 00:58:24,276
Yeah, feeling good about it.

454
00:58:26,695 --> 00:58:28,030
Hand me a plate.

455
00:58:28,322 --> 00:58:29,323
Sure.

456
00:58:42,753 --> 00:58:44,338
What’s with the smile?

457
00:58:47,341 --> 00:58:51,345
I haven’t seen you excited like this
in a long time.

458
00:58:53,639 --> 00:58:54,890
Am I?

459
00:58:59,895 --> 00:59:03,399
Looking forward to it.
Break a leg.

460
00:59:19,748 --> 00:59:21,458
Are you going to put her down?

461
00:59:24,086 --> 00:59:26,088
You know our center’s against that.

462
00:59:27,005 --> 00:59:28,692
Got any other ideas?

463
00:59:28,716 --> 00:59:32,010
She’ll be euthanized
no matter who catches her.

464
00:59:37,057 --> 00:59:38,392
But…

465
00:59:40,561 --> 00:59:41,498
Right away?

466
00:59:41,522 --> 00:59:43,774
We’re not going to kill her.

467
00:59:46,567 --> 00:59:50,362
She’s made it this far,
alone in the mountain.

468
00:59:52,364 --> 00:59:55,784
So what’s your plan?
Are you gonna raise her?

469
00:59:59,747 --> 01:00:02,875
You know I can’t.
Others would find out.

470
01:00:04,793 --> 01:00:08,464
We’re the only people
who come in here.

471
01:00:10,048 --> 01:00:12,509
I’ll make sure
no one else comes inside.

472
01:00:20,809 --> 01:00:22,102
Hayoung.

473
01:01:34,424 --> 01:01:35,968
How did you know?

474
01:01:37,511 --> 01:01:38,488
Know what?

475
01:01:38,512 --> 01:01:41,682
That I want to train her again.

476
01:01:44,935 --> 01:01:46,353
It just…

477
01:01:46,979 --> 01:01:49,690
seemed obvious while watching you.

478
01:01:57,531 --> 01:01:59,533
Don’t watch me anymore.

479
01:02:00,659 --> 01:02:01,702
Sorry?

480
01:02:02,452 --> 01:02:04,538
You said you were watching me.

481
01:02:06,832 --> 01:02:09,793
I don’t like being watched.

482
01:02:11,503 --> 01:02:12,713
Oh.

483
01:02:16,466 --> 01:02:17,634
Okay.

484
01:02:44,453 --> 01:02:47,015
How could you do that
without consulting me?

485
01:02:47,039 --> 01:02:49,917
You embarrassed me
in front of a coworker.

486
01:02:53,086 --> 01:02:56,006
Why are you staring at me like that?
Am I wrong?

487
01:03:00,135 --> 01:03:02,596
I tried to wake you yesterday,
but you were out cold.

488
01:03:04,389 --> 01:03:06,475
You were hammered.

489
01:03:09,603 --> 01:03:11,605
Our apprentices saw you.

490
01:03:12,689 --> 01:03:13,689
Huh?

491
01:03:20,572 --> 01:03:23,325
I guess you’ve been on edge
because of Tofu.

492
01:03:24,242 --> 01:03:26,119
And you’ve been working hard.

493
01:03:27,955 --> 01:03:31,541
We caught Tofu,
so it’s all settled now.

494
01:03:32,292 --> 01:03:33,794
What’s the problem?

495
01:03:35,921 --> 01:03:37,464
It’s not that.

496
01:03:38,715 --> 01:03:40,008
It’s you and me.

497
01:03:41,134 --> 01:03:43,387
Why are you so distant these days?

498
01:03:47,724 --> 01:03:50,936
Each time you stare at me like that… I…

499
01:03:51,687 --> 01:03:54,398
I don’t know what to do.

500
01:04:07,202 --> 01:04:09,579
There’s no “what” to it.

501
01:04:11,456 --> 01:04:13,792
Just do what you have to do.

502
01:04:16,670 --> 01:04:18,505
Or throw in the towel.

503
01:04:22,968 --> 01:04:24,678
Stick it out till the end.

504
01:05:19,524 --> 01:05:22,402
Look how soft your hair is now.

505
01:05:26,740 --> 01:05:27,908
Be still!

506
01:05:35,624 --> 01:05:37,626
What are you smiling about?

507
01:05:38,752 --> 01:05:39,961
Remember?

508
01:05:40,212 --> 01:05:43,507
You used to tie my hair like this
when we were kids.

509
01:05:44,466 --> 01:05:48,762
Your hair was so soft,
felt nice to touch it.

510
01:05:52,432 --> 01:05:56,645
When I stroked your hair
you would fall right asleep.

511
01:05:56,853 --> 01:05:58,605
Cut it out. That tickles.

512
01:06:05,737 --> 01:06:07,155
And now…

513
01:06:08,406 --> 01:06:10,408
that little girl’s all grown up.

514
01:06:14,788 --> 01:06:16,456
What do you mean?

515
01:06:18,416 --> 01:06:22,045
Oh you know. Isn’t it funny
that we live together now?

516
01:06:23,463 --> 01:06:25,215
Funny?

517
01:06:28,635 --> 01:06:29,803
I guess.

518
01:06:31,805 --> 01:06:33,807
Not what I expected either.

519
01:08:37,472 --> 01:08:45,472
<i>Happy birthday to you.</i>
<i>Happy birthday, dear Sora.</i>

520
01:08:50,151 --> 01:08:50,713
Happy birthday.

521
01:08:50,737 --> 01:08:52,247
<i>Thanks for being here</i>
Happy birthday.

522
01:08:54,281 --> 01:08:56,283
Hurry up.
The candle’s melting.

523
01:09:12,674 --> 01:09:14,259
You’re pretty fast.

524
01:09:15,302 --> 01:09:16,636
Hardly.

525
01:09:29,149 --> 01:09:30,400
Ta-da!

526
01:09:31,109 --> 01:09:33,546
You bought booze?
What’s gotten into you?

527
01:09:33,570 --> 01:09:35,488
Can’t have a party without booze.

528
01:09:37,699 --> 01:09:39,051
Do you like to drink?

529
01:09:39,075 --> 01:09:40,285
Of course.

530
01:09:44,956 --> 01:09:46,583
Will this be enough?

531
01:09:47,292 --> 01:09:49,252
I’ve been meaning to ask you
something.

532
01:09:49,669 --> 01:09:50,688
Let’s drink tonight.

533
01:09:50,712 --> 01:09:52,088
What is it?

534
01:09:53,423 --> 01:09:57,218
Why did you scream and
run away the other day?

535
01:09:58,762 --> 01:10:00,221
Oh…

536
01:10:02,682 --> 01:10:05,202
It just reminded me of something.

537
01:10:05,226 --> 01:10:06,394
What?

538
01:10:09,105 --> 01:10:13,652
When I was young,
I saw a wild dog at night.

539
01:10:14,778 --> 01:10:18,615
Oh, you were traumatized.

540
01:10:20,116 --> 01:10:22,118
But it wasn’t a dog.

541
01:10:23,870 --> 01:10:24,954
What was it?

542
01:10:27,165 --> 01:10:28,500
A person.

543
01:10:31,795 --> 01:10:34,357
Should I go buy some booze?

544
01:10:34,381 --> 01:10:35,816
Yeah, sure.

545
01:10:35,840 --> 01:10:37,276
What do you like?

546
01:10:37,300 --> 01:10:38,361
Liquor for me.

547
01:10:38,385 --> 01:10:39,385
Liquor!

548
01:11:11,209 --> 01:11:12,710
Having fun?

549
01:11:13,878 --> 01:11:17,090
Sure, join us.
Why are you out here alone?

550
01:11:19,717 --> 01:11:21,469
This is fun too.

551
01:11:25,223 --> 01:11:26,599
Can I join you?

552
01:11:29,853 --> 01:11:30,979
Why not.

553
01:11:59,591 --> 01:12:03,928
It’s like watching a play, isn’t it?

554
01:12:30,497 --> 01:12:31,891
You’re giving them a ride?

555
01:12:31,915 --> 01:12:33,917
Yeah, I didn’t drink.

556
01:12:35,919 --> 01:12:39,422
Throw a blanket over Sora.
She’ll catch a cold.

557
01:12:39,881 --> 01:12:40,924
Huh?

558
01:12:41,049 --> 01:12:42,485
Let’s go.

559
01:12:42,509 --> 01:12:43,611
Good night.

560
01:12:43,635 --> 01:12:45,321
Get home safe.

561
01:12:45,345 --> 01:12:47,406
<i>Au revoir.</i>

562
01:12:47,430 --> 01:12:49,474
- See you in a bit.
- Yeah, drive safe.

563
01:13:06,449 --> 01:13:07,927
Hayoung.

564
01:13:07,951 --> 01:13:09,077
Yes?

565
01:13:09,744 --> 01:13:16,042
Aren’t Yoonho and Sora
a bit too close?

566
01:13:17,669 --> 01:13:19,671
It’s nice for a family to be close.

567
01:13:22,590 --> 01:13:26,344
Seungjae, do you mind
if I drop her off first?

568
01:13:27,011 --> 01:13:28,096
Sure.

569
01:13:29,472 --> 01:13:33,434
Me? Go home?

570
01:13:34,602 --> 01:13:41,276
No way, I’m not going home.
Stop. Here, let me out here.

571
01:13:46,990 --> 01:13:49,784
Is it alright to leave her?

572
01:13:51,035 --> 01:13:53,204
I’m just glad to be rid of her.

573
01:13:54,080 --> 01:13:55,123
Huh?

574
01:13:57,458 --> 01:14:01,796
Shall we get some fresh air?

575
01:14:03,590 --> 01:14:05,300
Yes, I’d like that.

576
01:14:34,203 --> 01:14:40,001
Cut it out!
I told you. Don’t do that.

577
01:14:43,504 --> 01:14:44,797
Is that funny?

578
01:14:50,845 --> 01:14:53,348
What’s the big deal?
Hayoung does it all the time.

579
01:14:55,141 --> 01:14:56,601
But I can’t?

580
01:15:51,823 --> 01:15:55,118
<i>Sisters Survive House Fire</i>
<i>1998 Fire Started by Playing Children</i>

581
01:15:59,163 --> 01:16:01,600
<i>Sisters Left Behind by Father</i>

582
01:16:01,624 --> 01:16:05,253
<i>House Fire Started by Candle</i>

583
01:16:28,651 --> 01:16:30,254
What are you doing?

584
01:16:30,278 --> 01:16:32,363
Why are you reading all this?

585
01:16:33,072 --> 01:16:35,509
Hayoung, calm down.
Just hear me out.

586
01:16:35,533 --> 01:16:37,910
Is your book about me?

587
01:16:39,787 --> 01:16:42,832
Is that a problem?

588
01:16:47,378 --> 01:16:49,005
That’s my story.

589
01:16:49,380 --> 01:16:54,469
It’s not just your story.
Besides, it’s only a grain of inspiration.

590
01:17:02,226 --> 01:17:03,811
Oh, come on!

591
01:17:06,689 --> 01:17:11,778
It’s my novel.
I don’t need anyone’s permission!

592
01:17:29,545 --> 01:17:31,005
Don’t write it.

593
01:17:33,591 --> 01:17:34,884
Got that?

594
01:17:37,720 --> 01:17:39,806
Don’t tell me what to do.

595
01:18:10,461 --> 01:18:12,463
What are you playing at?

596
01:18:13,089 --> 01:18:18,302
Aren’t you curious?
What others thought about that day?

597
01:18:18,553 --> 01:18:22,807
We were playing with fire.
What’s there to think about?

598
01:18:23,558 --> 01:18:24,767
We?

599
01:18:32,942 --> 01:18:35,695
Why d’you teach me
how to start a fire that day?

600
01:18:41,576 --> 01:18:43,870
Why d’you leave me and run away?

601
01:18:56,340 --> 01:19:00,344
What did you come here for?

602
01:19:04,640 --> 01:19:08,019
You’re really lucky, you know?

603
01:19:10,396 --> 01:19:14,066
Living such a good life
after killing someone.

604
01:19:19,864 --> 01:19:21,699
What are you talking about?

605
01:19:24,785 --> 01:19:30,541
Sis, I learned
all my tricks from you.

606
01:21:35,332 --> 01:21:36,375
No!

607
01:21:44,508 --> 01:21:45,801
Good girl.

608
01:21:49,180 --> 01:21:50,180
Attagirl.

609
01:22:00,941 --> 01:22:04,987
Gonna let you off now. It’s okay.

610
01:22:29,386 --> 01:22:31,138
Wanna go out?

611
01:22:33,599 --> 01:22:35,434
I wish I could let you.

612
01:23:35,578 --> 01:23:37,246
Oh, Hayoung.

613
01:23:37,621 --> 01:23:38,789
Hey!

614
01:23:45,880 --> 01:23:48,465
Aw, thanks.
I’m so thirsty.

615
01:23:53,596 --> 01:23:56,432
Get it together. Come on!

616
01:24:03,606 --> 01:24:06,126
Hey, you’re here early.

617
01:24:06,150 --> 01:24:06,801
Yeah.

618
01:24:06,825 --> 01:24:08,327
Hello.

619
01:24:08,485 --> 01:24:09,174
Hello.

620
01:24:09,198 --> 01:24:11,450
- Our CEO.
- Nice to meet you.

621
01:24:15,159 --> 01:24:18,537
Have you read it already?
It’s only been a day.

622
01:24:19,538 --> 01:24:21,123
Oh, your book?

623
01:24:23,083 --> 01:24:25,085
Why horror all of a sudden?

624
01:24:26,128 --> 01:24:29,089
What did you think?
You can be honest.

625
01:24:29,423 --> 01:24:35,387
Actually, we called you in to talk about
a different project, not your book.

626
01:24:35,846 --> 01:24:38,599
Is there anything to discuss
besides my book?

627
01:24:39,516 --> 01:24:45,648
Well, we’d like you to write
essays for our website.

628
01:24:45,981 --> 01:24:48,817
Essays? Me?

629
01:24:49,818 --> 01:24:54,990
Your wife is trainer Lee Hayoung.
I’m a big fan of hers.

630
01:24:55,157 --> 01:24:59,078
I heard you met during an interview,
fell in love and got married.

631
01:25:00,579 --> 01:25:01,747
So?

632
01:25:04,124 --> 01:25:08,104
Basically, you’d write about
your daily life

633
01:25:08,128 --> 01:25:11,757
as a stay-at-home novelist
married to a famous dog trainer.

634
01:25:12,341 --> 01:25:13,509
What?

635
01:25:14,843 --> 01:25:18,347
Come on, you’re good at this.
It’s like a romantic diary.

636
01:25:19,223 --> 01:25:21,475
You used to blog all the time.

637
01:25:22,393 --> 01:25:26,438
That was years ago.
I stopped after my debut novel.

638
01:25:26,939 --> 01:25:32,027
If your essays are well received,
it could be a big help for your next book.

639
01:25:32,945 --> 01:25:36,115
So, how about it?

640
01:25:41,245 --> 01:25:45,165
Hello, everyone. I’m Lee Hayoung
from the Gureum Training Center.

641
01:25:48,335 --> 01:25:52,256
We’ll start with clicker training.

642
01:25:53,549 --> 01:25:56,736
Our friends need to know
this sound means “well done”, okay?

643
01:25:56,760 --> 01:25:57,946
Yes!

644
01:25:57,970 --> 01:25:58,987
So…

645
01:26:03,767 --> 01:26:05,561
Byeol, look at that!

646
01:26:06,520 --> 01:26:07,938
Hailey, touch.

647
01:26:13,152 --> 01:26:14,629
Do you all have your clickers?

648
01:26:14,653 --> 01:26:16,047
Yes.

649
01:26:16,071 --> 01:26:19,658
Let’s split up into groups
and start the clicker training.

650
01:26:20,117 --> 01:26:21,219
Yes.

651
01:26:21,243 --> 01:26:22,056
Give them a hand.

652
01:26:22,080 --> 01:26:25,375
The group session will last 20 minutes.

653
01:26:25,998 --> 01:26:30,002
You’re a little close together.
Give yourselves some room.

654
01:26:42,514 --> 01:26:44,058
Good.

655
01:27:25,432 --> 01:27:26,892
You’re doing great.

656
01:27:38,612 --> 01:27:40,465
Hello, ma’am.

657
01:27:40,489 --> 01:27:42,157
Hello.

658
01:27:42,825 --> 01:27:44,535
How have you been?

659
01:27:55,546 --> 01:27:57,631
I’m not going to give up on him.

660
01:28:01,927 --> 01:28:03,554
Start by believing in yourself.

661
01:28:08,016 --> 01:28:09,852
Okay, I’ll try.

662
01:28:11,478 --> 01:28:13,063
I’ll help you.

663
01:28:20,612 --> 01:28:22,614
Wanna go for a walk?

664
01:28:24,032 --> 01:28:25,284
Walkies!

665
01:28:33,250 --> 01:28:34,751
You have to keep at it.

666
01:28:41,717 --> 01:28:43,635
It’s okay. Don’t worry.

667
01:28:57,274 --> 01:28:59,359
What’s that?

668
01:28:59,902 --> 01:29:01,778
Oh my god!

669
01:29:06,116 --> 01:29:08,118
Let’s go!

670
01:30:06,009 --> 01:30:07,070
Take a rest.

671
01:30:07,094 --> 01:30:08,387
Thank you.

672
01:30:26,113 --> 01:30:27,489
Why are you here?

673
01:30:28,740 --> 01:30:30,284
Don’t be like that.

674
01:30:44,756 --> 01:30:46,174
What’s with you?

675
01:30:49,219 --> 01:30:51,972
It hurts to see you like this.

676
01:30:57,853 --> 01:31:02,024
My, look how sensitive you are.

677
01:31:04,526 --> 01:31:06,194
You mean it, right?

678
01:31:08,655 --> 01:31:09,948
Fuck off.

679
01:31:11,366 --> 01:31:12,826
You fucking dog.

680
01:31:23,003 --> 01:31:25,672
Ah, you’re home.

681
01:31:27,549 --> 01:31:29,092
Where’s Hayoung?

682
01:31:29,843 --> 01:31:31,511
You know she’s in the hospital.

683
01:31:36,016 --> 01:31:38,852
Who gets hospitalized for
a little nibble?

684
01:31:39,770 --> 01:31:40,896
Such a drama queen.

685
01:31:42,689 --> 01:31:44,524
And whose fault is that?

686
01:31:48,945 --> 01:31:52,324
It’s my fault, right?
I bit her.

687
01:32:04,878 --> 01:32:07,839
You know what’s inside
that warehouse at the center?

688
01:32:08,548 --> 01:32:10,884
See the news?
About that wild dog?

689
01:32:11,385 --> 01:32:13,387
Now that one really bit someone.

690
01:32:13,929 --> 01:32:17,307
And if it kills someone,
it’ll be a killer dog.

691
01:32:18,642 --> 01:32:22,312
So Hayoung will be the trainer
who trained a killer dog.

692
01:32:25,023 --> 01:32:26,525
I’m not drinking.

693
01:32:40,622 --> 01:32:42,624
It’s an idea for your book.

694
01:32:43,458 --> 01:32:45,127
Not interested.

695
01:32:48,588 --> 01:32:50,132
Then how about this.

696
01:32:52,175 --> 01:32:54,177
Wanna run away with me?

697
01:33:18,034 --> 01:33:20,328
Or write about mooching off my sister.

698
01:33:22,622 --> 01:33:23,749
What?

699
01:33:25,000 --> 01:33:26,269
It’s true.

700
01:33:26,293 --> 01:33:29,045
You can’t write a word
without her permission.

701
01:33:53,028 --> 01:33:55,030
You think I’m pathetic?

702
01:33:55,947 --> 01:33:56,990
What?

703
01:33:58,033 --> 01:34:02,120
You’re the one who’s pathetic.

704
01:34:05,040 --> 01:34:07,042
The secret behind the blaze,

705
01:34:07,542 --> 01:34:10,670
the older sister killing her father
and setting the fire.

706
01:34:11,505 --> 01:34:13,757
I wrote about that.

707
01:34:16,760 --> 01:34:19,137
But it didn’t make any sense.

708
01:34:24,309 --> 01:34:28,730
She had no reason to kill her father.

709
01:34:29,731 --> 01:34:33,777
I saw it with my own eyes.

710
01:34:35,904 --> 01:34:38,198
That’s not important.

711
01:34:39,115 --> 01:34:42,953
I’m talking about
the logic of the story.

712
01:34:44,120 --> 01:34:49,042
When you look at it all together
there’s only one solution.

713
01:34:53,922 --> 01:34:58,218
The younger sister killed him
and pretends otherwise.

714
01:35:00,095 --> 01:35:01,096
Why?

715
01:35:01,429 --> 01:35:03,723
Because she wants to blame others.

716
01:35:04,516 --> 01:35:06,226
She feels…

717
01:35:08,353 --> 01:35:10,689
her life has been unfair.

718
01:35:13,984 --> 01:35:16,820
You don’t know a thing about me.

719
01:35:20,866 --> 01:35:22,534
Of course not.

720
01:35:23,368 --> 01:35:25,829
I would just write it that way.

721
01:35:36,089 --> 01:35:39,050
I deactivated Tofu’s microchip.

722
01:35:43,263 --> 01:35:47,934
There’s no evidence that
she was trained by you.

723
01:35:53,565 --> 01:35:58,236
Maybe we should free her
back into the mountains?

724
01:36:00,739 --> 01:36:03,575
I’m not sure what to do next.

725
01:36:08,455 --> 01:36:12,459
Seungjae, why are you
so eager to save her?

726
01:36:20,926 --> 01:36:22,510
I want to see.

727
01:36:23,219 --> 01:36:25,555
If she can really change.

728
01:36:31,937 --> 01:36:33,438
Why are you smiling?

729
01:37:39,337 --> 01:37:42,007
Let’s go.

730
01:38:18,501 --> 01:38:20,003
Yoonho?

731
01:38:21,629 --> 01:38:23,131
Yoonho!

732
01:38:35,435 --> 01:38:36,454
Hello?

733
01:38:36,478 --> 01:38:37,495
Hey!

734
01:38:38,229 --> 01:38:39,647
- Let go!
- Are you nuts?

735
01:38:40,732 --> 01:38:41,983
Get off!

736
01:38:46,613 --> 01:38:48,448
Let go of it!

737
01:38:59,834 --> 01:39:01,377
Give it to me!

738
01:39:21,106 --> 01:39:22,315
Sora.

739
01:39:26,903 --> 01:39:28,404
Put it down.

740
01:39:29,447 --> 01:39:31,616
Sora, listen to me.

741
01:39:33,159 --> 01:39:35,161
Why would I listen to you?

742
01:39:37,747 --> 01:39:39,415
So what’s your plan?

743
01:39:40,333 --> 01:39:42,127
How do you get away with this?

744
01:39:49,342 --> 01:39:52,220
He’s still alive. He’s not dead.

745
01:39:52,637 --> 01:39:55,390
This is an accident. Okay?

746
01:40:02,105 --> 01:40:04,107
Let’s call 911 right now.

747
01:40:04,566 --> 01:40:06,776
Then what about me?

748
01:40:07,652 --> 01:40:09,571
Am I going inside again?

749
01:40:10,947 --> 01:40:13,700
I’ll help you.

750
01:40:15,160 --> 01:40:17,680
We’ll go to the police together.

751
01:40:17,704 --> 01:40:21,624
Why is it always me
who gets punished!

752
01:40:25,378 --> 01:40:27,922
No! It’s not like that.

753
01:40:29,841 --> 01:40:31,301
It’s okay.

754
01:40:32,760 --> 01:40:37,182
It’ll all be okay.

755
01:40:39,934 --> 01:40:41,686
I’ll wait for you.

756
01:40:49,194 --> 01:40:51,529
I waited for you,
but you never came.

757
01:40:58,995 --> 01:41:00,997
I was scared too then.

758
01:41:02,457 --> 01:41:05,728
- I was so young.
- I was younger!

759
01:41:05,752 --> 01:41:07,754
You had me!

760
01:41:09,923 --> 01:41:12,091
I had no one.

761
01:41:58,388 --> 01:42:00,723
I’ll sort it out with Yoonho.

762
01:42:03,601 --> 01:42:06,145
They’ll take that into consideration.

763
01:42:09,524 --> 01:42:11,901
Just endure it for a little while
and come back.

764
01:42:14,279 --> 01:42:16,281
I’ll be right here.

765
01:42:38,011 --> 01:42:39,470
Sora!

766
01:42:44,267 --> 01:42:45,893
Sora!

767
01:42:56,946 --> 01:42:58,406
Lee Sora!

